; beancount's lexer reads a date as four or more digits, then twice a dash
; or a slash and digits, and takes each part as a number: every open below
; is dated like 2020-01-02, and the cost date and the metadata date are
; dates, not subtractions.
2020-1-2 open Assets:A
2020-01-002 open Assets:B
02020-01-02 open Assets:C
2020/01-02 open Assets:D
  when: 2020-010-2

2020-2-1 * "a cost dated loosely"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {5 USD, 2020-1-5}
  Assets:B  -5 USD

2020-02-02 balance Assets:B  -5 USD
